            <tr><td class="py-3 pr-4">audit_retention_years</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">5</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">Minimum audit retention period</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">Audit</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="py-3 pr-4">platform_admin_mfa_required</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">true</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">Require MFA for SaaS platform administrators</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">Platform admin, security</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="py-3 pr-4">support_access_expiry_minutes</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">60</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">Maximum approved support impersonation session duration</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">Support, audit</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="py-3 pr-4">allow_platform_admin_direct_data_access</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">false</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">Emergency-only break-glass operational data access; disabled by default and must be audited if ever enabled</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">Platform admin, compliance</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="out-of-scope" class="prose prose-zinc max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
      <h2>9. Out of scope</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Full accounting suite beyond finance-lite summary, supplier payable visibility, and payment/shift reports.</li>
        <li>Advanced loyalty engine beyond customer groups and basic pricing segmentation.</li>
        <li>Marketplace integration, delivery integration, online ordering, and e-commerce storefront.</li>
        <li>Custom approval workflow UI builder; v1 uses predefined config flags, not custom workflow design.</li>
        <li>Direct SIPNAP API integration; manual report export is sufficient for v1.</li>
        <li>Medical-record, clinic, doctor, diagnosis, patient, or e-prescription workflow as a core module.</li>
        <li>Any workflow not specific to pharmacy operations.</li>
        <li>Temperature/IOT monitoring and distributor-grade CDOB certification suite.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="roadmap" class="prose prose-zinc max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
      <h2>10. Build order and milestones</h2>
      <h3>Phase 0 — Foundation</h3>
      <p><strong>Deliverables:</strong> app shell, database migrations, tenant model, auth, MFA for owner/support/platform admin, tenant RBAC, platform-admin role, platform audit-log base, support impersonation model, CI, seed data, billing state model.</p>
      <p><strong>Definition of done:</strong> a tenant can register, create default outlet/warehouse, invite users, assign roles, and pass tenant isolation tests. A Platform Admin can view tenant metadata and billing/plan status without opening operational pharmacy records. CI runs lint/typecheck/test/build.</p>
      <p><strong>Regulatory included:</strong> audit foundation and tenant-isolated sensitive records.</p>

      <h3>Phase 1 — Core master data and ledger</h3>
      <p><strong>Deliverables:</strong> product master, unit conversions, suppliers/PBF, pricing/history, stock_batches, stock_movements, posting service, stock card, opening stock import.</p>
      <p><strong>Definition of done:</strong> opening stock can be imported, movements reconcile to batch balances, unit conversion tests pass, and posted movements cannot be silently edited.</p>
      <p><strong>Regulatory included:</strong> product compliance flags, batch/expiry fields, audit of price and stock changes.</p>

      <h3>Phase 2 — Procurement and stock control</h3>
      <p><strong>Deliverables:</strong> defecta, PO, SP document types, goods receipt, partial fulfillment, PBF invoice fields, purchase return, stock take, transfer, expiry quarantine, disposal.</p>
      <p><strong>Definition of done:</strong> a user can create defecta, convert to PO, generate required SP, receive partial goods with batch/expiry/invoice, post ledger movements, run stock take, quarantine expired goods, and dispose with audit trail.</p>
      <p><strong>Regulatory included:</strong> SP Obat Keras/Narkotika/Psikotropika/Precursor, PBF faktur fields, quarantine/disposal traceability.</p>

      <h3>Phase 3 — POS and shift</h3>
      <p><strong>Deliverables:</strong> shift open/close, product search/barcode, cart, discounts, mixed payment, bon, regulated item gates, FEFO stock deduction, receipt customization, refunds/voids, offline POS minimum mode.</p>
      <p><strong>Definition of done:</strong> cashier can complete normal sale under 45 seconds, mixed payment sale posts correctly, bon requires customer and creates receivable, restricted products require gate, and offline sale sync either posts or enters conflict review without silent ledger corruption.</p>
      <p><strong>Regulatory included:</strong> checkout gate for obat keras/resep and regulated item audit trail.</p>

      <h3>Phase 4 — Reports, dashboards, audit trail</h3>
      <p><strong>Deliverables:</strong> owner/admin/cashier/procurement dashboards, stock reports, sales reports, purchase reports, finance-lite, expiry loss, SIPNAP-ready export, audit filters, CSV/XLSX/PDF exports.</p>
      <p><strong>Definition of done:</strong> all launch metrics can be measured, reports reconcile to ledger, role visibility is enforced, and monthly regulated item export is generated from movement data.</p>
      <p><strong>Regulatory included:</strong> SIPNAP-ready monthly export and regulatory movement report.</p>

      <h3>Phase 5 — Onboarding, billing, SaaS polish</h3>
      <p><strong>Deliverables:</strong> self-serve onboarding checklist, import templates, demo data, billing plan enforcement, data export package, support impersonation approval, backup/restore runbook, production monitoring.</p>
      <p><strong>Definition of done:</strong> a small pharmacy can go from registration to first live sale in under 2 hours, owner can export full tenant data, suspended tenant remains export-capable during grace period, and restore drill meets RPO/RTO targets.</p>
      <p><strong>Regulatory included:</strong> retention policy, export audit, sensitive record security review.</p>
    </section>

